xfs: lift a xfs_valid_startblock into xfs_bmapi_allocate

jira KERNEL-1630
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.166.1.el8_10
commit-author Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
commit 04c609e6e5066294b60329420d3711e990c47abf
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.166.1.el8_10/04c609e6.failed

xfs_bmapi_convert_delalloc has a xfs_valid_startblock check on the block
allocated by xfs_bmapi_allocate.  Lift it into xfs_bmapi_allocate as
we should assert the same for xfs_bmapi_write.

	Signed-off-by: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
	Reviewed-by: "Darrick J. Wong" <djwong@kernel.org>
	Signed-off-by: Chandan Babu R <chandanbabu@kernel.org>
(cherry picked from commit 04c609e6e5066294b60329420d3711e990c47abf)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/xfs/libxfs/xfs_bmap.c
diff --cc fs/xfs/libxfs/xfs_bmap.c
index fec2e85cbd25,eade9689599f..000000000000
--- a/fs/xfs/libxfs/xfs_bmap.c
+++ b/fs/xfs/libxfs/xfs_bmap.c
@@@ -4610,10 -4718,6 +4615,13 @@@ xfs_bmapi_convert_delalloc
  	if (error)
  		goto out_finish;
  
++<<<<<<< HEAD
 +	error = -EFSCORRUPTED;
 +	if (WARN_ON_ONCE(!xfs_valid_startblock(ip, bma.got.br_startblock)))
 +		goto out_finish;
 +
++=======
++>>>>>>> 04c609e6e506 (xfs: lift a xfs_valid_startblock into xfs_bmapi_allocate)
  	XFS_STATS_ADD(mp, xs_xstrat_bytes, XFS_FSB_TO_B(mp, bma.length));
  	XFS_STATS_INC(mp, xs_xstrat_quick);
  
* Unmerged path fs/xfs/libxfs/xfs_bmap.c
